WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.960
A bright flash of light awakes Pietro Wilson from&nbsp;
his vegetative state. He sits up and brushes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:10.640
sand off himself, looking around the desolate&nbsp;
desert he’s found himself in. How did he get here?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:16.000
The last thing he remembers is uncovering secret&nbsp;
orders from the leaders of the SCP Foundation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.640
just before they declared war on humanity.&nbsp;
Unfortunately, the most important parts of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.240
files had been redacted. Now he's on a mission to&nbsp;
finally discover why the SCP Foundation is trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.280
to kill every last human on the planet... but&nbsp;
there is something else he has to deal with first.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:37.040
“What happened?” Pietro says out loud as he looks&nbsp;
at his vitals in the heads up display of SCP-5000.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:42.480
He is still contained within the exclusionary&nbsp;
suit that makes him undetectable to human senses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:48.560
He checks the date and gasps in surprise. “Three&nbsp;
months! I’ve been passed out for three months!”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:53.600
He stands up and looks across the&nbsp;
barren landscape. The screen inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:58.480
the suit indicates he has traversed half of the&nbsp;
country since he left Site-19 three months ago.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:03.840
Pietro looks down at one of his hands. He is&nbsp;
holding a black leather briefcase. “Where did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:08.480
that come from?” he wonders. Pietro has&nbsp;
no idea what is inside the briefcase,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.720
but he knows it definitely isn’t&nbsp;
round. He tries to let it go,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:18.160
his fingers won’t open. He uses his other hand&nbsp;
to try and pry the briefcase away from himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:24.720
but his hand only clasps to it harder. Then a wave&nbsp;
of calm washes over him. Something inside his head&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:31.200
speaks to him, but it’s not a voice, more like a&nbsp;
feeling. It is a sense of purpose, and Pietro’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:38.720
new mission in life is to deliver this briefcase&nbsp;
to SCP-579, nothing else is as important.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.160
Pietro Wilson takes a deep breath and embraces his&nbsp;
new purpose in life. He still wants to uncover the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:49.360
reason that the SCP Foundation is trying to wipe&nbsp;
out humanity, but this will have to wait until&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:56.880
he delivers the briefcase to SCP-579. Pietro&nbsp;
does not know exactly where 579 is located, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:03.280
he can feel a pull in a certain direction, so he&nbsp;
begins to walk. Pietro brings up the information&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:09.840
stored in the SCP-5000 suit from the Foundation’s&nbsp;
database. He finds that all information about what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:15.360
SCP-579 is has been expunged from the record.&nbsp;
The only useful information in the file is that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:22.320
the Keter level SCP is located at Site-62c.&nbsp;
At least Pietro has a destination to aim for.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:27.520
He travels for days without seeing a living&nbsp;
soul. But he does pass thousands of corpses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:32.640
He tries to ignore them but one stands out to&nbsp;
him inside a house as he searches for supplies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.640
It's the body of a recently deceased boy. He&nbsp;
couldn't have been more than eight years old.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:46.480
He was so young, Pietro thinks. He bends over&nbsp;
to scoop up the body and bury it outside. As&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:52.160
his hand touches the body, the boy’s skin begins&nbsp;
to move. It is as if hundreds of tiny creatures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.160 --> 00:02:58.080
are scurrying just under the skin. Then, from out&nbsp;
of every orifice, comes hundreds of little pale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:04.240
worms. each with the face of the boy. They are&nbsp;
all cackling as they crawl off the boy’s body and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:11.040
into a drain a few feet away. Pietro jumps back&nbsp;
and runs. That is the last person I try to bury,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:16.960
he thinks. Pietro pushes forward, the hundreds&nbsp;
of little laughing worms haunting his thoughts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:21.440
until he puts a significant distance&nbsp;
between himself and the little boy’s body.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.560
Pietro continues to walk towards the direction of&nbsp;
Site-62c. He passes more corpses, but decides to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.760
stay clear of them. Although the suit makes it&nbsp;
so Pietro doesn’t need to rest, he can only go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:39.760
so fast. He enters a small abandoned town that&nbsp;
looks like something out of an old western movie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:45.200
A tumbleweed blows across the dirt road. Pietro&nbsp;
sits on the wooden step of the local saloon and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.480
takes a break. He looks down at the briefcase&nbsp;
in his hand. He hasn’t had the urge to open it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:57.040
only to deliver it to SCP-579. Pietro puts the&nbsp;
black briefcase on his lap. He stares at it and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:02.640
slides his hands along the leather, stops with his&nbsp;
thumb on the latch, and pushes. The silver locks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:08.640
snap open. Pietro opens the briefcase... a&nbsp;
bright light beams out, and he passes out.

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:16.480
When Pietro comes to again he is miles closer to&nbsp;
Site-62c. There is a warm feeling enveloping his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:22.480
body. He looks down at the briefcase which is now&nbsp;
closed. Wow, this thing is like my own personal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:29.280
skip button, Pietro thinks. He holds up the&nbsp;
briefcase, unlatches the locks, sees the bright&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:35.840
light, and passes out again. He awakes once again&nbsp;
miles away from his last position. So it wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:41.280
just a one-off effect. Pietro continues walking&nbsp;
across the country, switching between using his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:47.120
own legs and whatever magic is contained within&nbsp;
the briefcase. He is making faster progress now.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:52.880
As he walks through a dense deciduous forest he&nbsp;
comes across a pack of wolves eating the remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:59.040
of an SCP Agent. Pietro is undetectable&nbsp;
to the wolves thanks to the SCP-5000 suit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:03.680
and he makes his way over to the pack, quietly&nbsp;
grabbing a laptop laying on the ground next to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:09.200
the agent’s body. Pietro takes the laptop and goes&nbsp;
a way deeper into the forest before stopping to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:14.640
boot up the computer. He has not forgotten about&nbsp;
the horrors the SCP Foundation has released and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.640 --> 00:05:22.400
he needs to know how the world has been doing over&nbsp;
the last few months. What he finds is... not good.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:28.480
The SCP Foundation has triggered the eruption of&nbsp;
Yellowstone destroying SCP-2000, which unknown to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:33.520
Pietro, contained the failsafe for rebuilding&nbsp;
human society in the event of a world ending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:39.760
scenario, which this was starting to look more and&nbsp;
more like. It was only a matter of time now before&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:44.720
the soot and ash thrown up by the eruption blocks&nbsp;
out the sun in much of what is left of the United&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:52.560
States. The Foundation has also found a way to get&nbsp;
SCP-2241 to do their dirty work at refugee camps.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:57.600
The young brown haired boy is most likely being&nbsp;
manipulated by the Foundation under the pretenses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.880
that they are only doing what’s best for “their”&nbsp;
child. He has caused whole groups of refugees to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.760
turn on eachother, leading to a massacre.&nbsp;
The last entry says that the young boy is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:12.560
being sent to the The Global Occult Coalition&nbsp;
hold out at Ganzir, to help destroy some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:18.240
last threats to the SCP Foundation. A series of&nbsp;
other SCPs have been dispatched by the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:23.680
around the world to continue the destruction&nbsp;
of humanity. They even managed to use temporal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:31.120
anomalies to make it Christmas time everywhere&nbsp;
around the world so SCP-4666, the brutal Yule-tide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:37.760
creature that stalks the homes of children, is&nbsp;
free to cause chaos. Pietro had seen enough.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:44.240
He slams the laptop shut, throws it against the&nbsp;
trunk of a tree., and opens the briefcase again.

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:48.800
He awakes standing feet away from a group&nbsp;
of Global Occult Coalition soldiers who are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.760
sitting around a campfire. Maybe they know why&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation is trying to end the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.760 --> 00:06:58.000
he thinks. He decides that it is too&nbsp;
risky to show himself to the soldiers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:03.600
but takes some solace in sitting around the&nbsp;
campfire with other living humans. The soldiers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:08.160
are sharing stories about what is happening,&nbsp;
one catches the attention of Pietro Wilson.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:15.520
It is strange, but also may hold a clue as to why&nbsp;
the SCP Foundation is trying to wipe out humanity.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.520
One of the soldiers recounts an event that&nbsp;
he witnessed before leaving the Global Occult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:25.280
Coalition’s headquarters at Ganzir. They had just&nbsp;
captured an SCP soldier trying to break into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:32.080
base. The infiltrator's name was Samuel Ross.&nbsp;
He had been strapped into an interrogation chair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:37.280
and questioned. The interviewers were not getting&nbsp;
anywhere until Ross was threatened with torture,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:43.280
to which he responded “Do what you want. Once&nbsp;
you realize you're not supposed to feel pain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:45.120
there's nothing to be afraid of anymore.”

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:48.880
Pietro sits up straight and&nbsp;
starts to listen more intently.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:54.960
He remembers stumbling across SCP soldiers on&nbsp;
his way to Site-19 that exhibited the same “no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:57.840
pain” mentality that this&nbsp;
Samuel Ross seems to have.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:05.040
After that odd statement by Samuel Ross there&nbsp;
was the sound of wind. It started slow at first,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:10.240
then ramped up until it was howling like a&nbsp;
hurricane. That’s when the screaming started.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:15.040
The screams became louder and climbed to&nbsp;
a higher pitch. Then the room went dead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:32.880
silent. The last thing that Samuel Ross said&nbsp;
was, “I really liked you guys, so I was trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:41.840
to be nice. We're so kind to you, you know. We&nbsp;
fight in the light so you can die in the dark.”

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:51.360
Pietro sits back on his haunches and rocks back&nbsp;
and forth. He has an ominous feeling that there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.360 --> 00:08:57.120
is a connection between the missing pain of the&nbsp;
SCP soldiers, and the reason why the Foundation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:02.480
declared war on humanity. The soldier who&nbsp;
told the story of Samual Ross stands up.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:07.280
“After that interview is when the destruction&nbsp;
of Ganzir started from the inside. It is why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:13.200
the Global Occult Coalition is no more. God help&nbsp;
us all.” The soldier, finished with his story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.200 --> 00:09:18.320
turns from the others and starts to walk away.&nbsp;
As the soldier makes his way towards the woods&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:23.520
Pietro can just barely make out that he’s taken&nbsp;
his pistol from its holster before he disappears&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:30.320
into the darkness. The world truly has gone&nbsp;
mad. Pietro opens the briefcase and blacks out.

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:35.120
Pietro sluggishly continues his walk. He’s&nbsp;
moving down a rocky path in the middle of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:41.360
forest and his will to keep going is slowly being&nbsp;
drained. The only reason he has not sat down and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.360 --> 00:09:49.200
given up is because of the driving urge to get the&nbsp;
briefcase to 579. He wants so badly to concentrate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:53.920
and discover the reason that the Foundation&nbsp;
released the SCPs on humanity, but the need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:59.520
to reach 579 won’t let him to focus on anything&nbsp;
else. He’s noticed though that every time he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:05.280
opens the briefcase to skip ahead, he makes less&nbsp;
and less progress. The warm feeling of the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:10.560
few transports has been replaced by a nauseated&nbsp;
headache every time he comes out of the trance.

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:16.080
Pietro exits the forest into an open field. The&nbsp;
wind blows across the high grass looking like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.080 --> 00:10:21.920
green waves, and standing scattered throughout&nbsp;
the field are statues. As Pietro approaches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:28.800
he sees that they are statues of Mobile Task Force&nbsp;
Foundation soldiers. He slowly walks closer to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.800 --> 00:10:35.120
white marble statues. He reaches the first one and&nbsp;
looks at the face of the frozen soldier, his eyes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.120 --> 00:10:42.320
have been scooped out, all that remains are black,&nbsp;
empty, sockets. The arms of the soldier have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:48.320
carved into blades, like a praying mantis. He&nbsp;
walks past the first statue and proceeds to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:54.480
next one when he hears something move in the grass&nbsp;
behind him. He spins around to look at the statue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.840
He could have swore it was in a slightly different&nbsp;
position. No, that’s crazy, Pietro thinks.

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:05.120
He continues to the next statue. It&nbsp;
is another carving of a MTF soldier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:13.520
no eyes, blades for arms. “This is really creepy,”&nbsp;
Pietro says aloud. He proceeds through the field.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.960
He walks up a slight hill and turns&nbsp;
around to look at the field of statues.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:23.120
What he sees is terrifying. The statues have&nbsp;
all moved and are now in different positions.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:29.200
It appears as if they were slashing through&nbsp;
the area looking for something… or someone.

00:11:29.840 --> 00:11:34.960
Pietro continues over the hill and comes upon&nbsp;
a group of refugees. They are picking through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.960 --> 00:11:40.080
the field looking for food to eat. A fog&nbsp;
begins to move in, it is being swept across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:45.280
the meadow by the wind. Pietro watches from a&nbsp;
distance as the fog envelopes the small group.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:51.520
Suddenly there is screaming and the sound of&nbsp;
blades going through flesh. The screams cease&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:57.920
almost immediately. Pietro runs down the hill to&nbsp;
where the refugees were. The fog lifts. The group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.920 --> 00:12:02.240
of people have been cut to pieces. Standing&nbsp;
in the middle of the carnage is one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:09.840
MTF soldier statues, blood dripping from its&nbsp;
blade arms. Pietro knows what to do… he runs.

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:15.280
After a few miles Pietro slows to catch his&nbsp;
breath. “Those statues must have been created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:20.720
by the Foundation” he thinks, “It’s as if they&nbsp;
are frozen in place, but as soon as you take your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:26.160
eyes off them they can move with killer speed.&nbsp;
Even in the suit my eyesight can stop them…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:26.160 --> 00:12:30.640
but they can’t see me… they must know&nbsp;
I’m there though since they can’t move.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.640 --> 00:12:36.240
Pietro Wilson opens the briefcase one again,&nbsp;
for what he didn’t know would be the last time.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:39.760
When he comes to this time he is near Site-62c.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:44.560
He can feel himself being pulled stronger than&nbsp;
ever in the direction of his destination. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:51.040
walks down a deserted road past the husks of burnt&nbsp;
vehicles and at the end is the gate to Site-62c.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:56.640
There are no guards or security of any kind. It&nbsp;
looks like the site has been abandoned for a long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:06.320
time and the gate is wide open, beckoning Pietro&nbsp;
Wilson into Site-62c... where SCP-579 waits.

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:12.800
Pietro Wilson enters the dark hallway he somehow&nbsp;
knows leads down into the crypt of Site-62c.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.800 --> 00:13:18.560
The walls drip with what he hopes is water from&nbsp;
leaking pipes, but it has a metallic smell, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.560 --> 00:13:26.000
is much too red to actually be water. He begins to&nbsp;
feel nauseous. It gets harder to breathe. Even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:32.583
SCP-5000 suit can’t keep him calm. He turns and&nbsp;
runs back up the stairs out of Site-62c. He stops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.583 --> 00:13:36.000
a few feet from the entryway, bends over, and&nbsp;
vomits. Pietro begins to sob uncontrollably as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:41.040
memories of everything that has happened over the&nbsp;
past several months suffocates his will to go on.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:48.640
Then, as if an invisible force that refuses to&nbsp;
let him go takes control. Pietro feels as if a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:54.160
gun has been shoved into the small of his&nbsp;
back. He is being sent back into Site-62c&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:54.160 --> 00:14:00.080
whether he wants to go or not. He is unsure&nbsp;
if what is forcing him back into the base is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:06.800
inside the briefcase, his own uncontrollable&nbsp;
urge to know what is going on, or SCP-579 itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:06.800 --> 00:14:12.720
but he cannot stop himself from re-entering&nbsp;
the doorway and preceding into Site-62c. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:12.720 --> 00:14:19.280
doesn’t know what SCP-579 looks like, but Pietro&nbsp;
has a sinister feeling that it is watching him.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:22.960
He reaches the bottom of the stairway&nbsp;
and proceeds down a dark hallway.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:29.040
The power went out long ago and the only light&nbsp;
in the depths of Site-62c is the dim glow coming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:29.040 --> 00:14:35.840
from the helmet of the SCP-5000 suit. Pietro&nbsp;
notices long gashes along the concrete walls,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:35.840 --> 00:14:40.320
as if someone took a giant knife and dragged&nbsp;
it from one end of the hallway to the other.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:43.600
There is something at the end of the&nbsp;
corridor that Pietro can’t make out.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:48.080
As he gets closer the lights on&nbsp;
the SCP-5000 suit begin to flicker.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:53.120
The thing at the end of the hallway seems to move&nbsp;
slightly each time the lights on the suit dim.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:15:00.400
The lights of the suit go out completely and the&nbsp;
entire hallway is plunged into darkness. Only for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:00.400 --> 00:15:05.680
a second though, and when the lights come back&nbsp;
on a statue of a MTF soldier looms over Pietro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:06.240 --> 00:15:10.080
its eyes are empty sockets, its&nbsp;
lips are turned up in a snarl,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:16.560
the arms have been filed into blades. “No!”&nbsp;
Pietro screams. He dodges around the statue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:16.560 --> 00:15:21.440
the moment it is out of his sight he hears the&nbsp;
sound of blades on concrete, as the statue of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:25.840
the soldier comes to life and begins slashing&nbsp;
its way down the hallway. It cannot see Pietro,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:26.480 --> 00:15:31.520
but it knows he is there. It slashes all around,&nbsp;
trying to connect with whoever is there with it.

00:15:32.320 --> 00:15:37.440
Pietro runs to the end of the hallway and reaches&nbsp;
a door. He presses against the heavy metal door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:43.440
open, straining against its weight all while the&nbsp;
blind statue is still slashing, coming closer and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:49.440
closer. The door is almost open, but then Pietro&nbsp;
feels a blade lacerate the back of the suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:49.440 --> 00:15:55.200
cutting deeply into the skin of his back, missing&nbsp;
his spinal cord by millimeters. Another blade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:59.520
enters through the back of his shoulder piercing&nbsp;
straight through. He somehow pulls himself through&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:04.480
the cracked doorway and kicks the metal door shut&nbsp;
behind him. He can hear the banging and scraping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:10.000
of blades outside of the metal door. The creature&nbsp;
has not given up and is trying to break in.

00:16:10.000 --> 00:16:15.040
Pietro turns around to see he is in an observation&nbsp;
chamber full of instruments and screens.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:15.840 --> 00:16:21.200
Blood runs down his back from the wounds inflicted&nbsp;
by the statue. He walks slowly over to the window,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:21.200 --> 00:16:26.800
on the desk in front of him is a file&nbsp;
labeled SCP-579. He looks through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:31.760
observation glass and down into the chamber&nbsp;
below. It is too dark to make anything out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:38.400
but Pietro can feel that SCP-579 is down there&nbsp;
looking up at him. Pietro looks to his left and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:44.160
sees a hole in the floor. He walks over and looks&nbsp;
down. It leads right into the containment chamber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:44.160 --> 00:16:50.720
of 579. “Let’s get this over with,” Pietro says&nbsp;
out loud. He holds the briefcase over the hole and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:50.720 --> 00:16:58.080
tries to open his hand. His finger won’t budge.&nbsp;
SCP-579 wants him to hand deliver the briefcase..

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:02.800
Pietro Wilson takes a deep breath, closes&nbsp;
his eyes, and steps into the opening of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:09.200
the hole. He falls. In the moments before&nbsp;
he lands in SCP-579’s containment chamber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:14.240
something comes to him. He realizes that he isn’t&nbsp;
going to be a hero, he isn’t going to figure out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:20.960
why the SCP Foundation is trying to wipe out&nbsp;
humanity… and he isn’t going to survive. He&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:20.960 --> 00:17:26.320
lands hard on the ground below. It is completely&nbsp;
dark, except for a shadow that moves in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:26.320 --> 00:17:31.840
corner of the containment chamber. Pietro Wilson&nbsp;
creates one last log, “if anyone ever reads this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:43.680
please, please, figure out why. Explain it to me.&nbsp;
Someone … anyone. I don't get it. I just don't get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:52.400
it…” SCP-579 steps into the glow that the SCP-5000&nbsp;
suit is giving off. Pietro Wilson looks up at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.400 --> 00:18:06.480
it. “Oh … so that's how it is.” he says before&nbsp;
SCP-5000 creates its final log: LIFE SIGNS LOST.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:13.760
SCP-5000 appeared in a flash of light&nbsp;
in the containment chamber of SCP-579&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:21.360
located in Site-62C. The researchers monitoring&nbsp;
SCP-579 had no idea where the suit came from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.360 --> 00:18:26.960
or why it contained the body of Pietro Wilson,&nbsp;
a foundation employee who is assigned to Site-06&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:32.320
and is very much alive. Wilson appears&nbsp;
to have no knowledge of SCP-5000&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:37.840
or memories of the events logged in SCP-5000’s&nbsp;
databanks. Although the suit is believed to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:41.760
been capable at one point of a number&nbsp;
of anomalous functions and abilities,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:46.960
the damage it has sustained has rendered it&nbsp;
inoperable except for the storage of data files,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:46.960 --> 00:18:51.280
which have now been archived and&nbsp;
stored on secure Foundation servers.

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.560
Now check out the earlier&nbsp;
episodes of Pietro Wilson&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:09.852
and SCP-5000 by watching SCP-5000 - The&nbsp;
Suit. Or watch SCP-106 - The Old Man Escape.

